# ── Real SAP exports — deliberately NOT committed ─────────────────────────
# Assets/ holds live procurement data: 368 named requisitioners, approver login
# identifiers and GR user names. That is personal data under the PDP Law
# (UU 27/2022), and git history is effectively permanent — removing it later
# means rewriting history everywhere the repo has been cloned.
#
# The application reads this folder as a read-only volume at runtime, so it does
# not need to be in the repo. For CI and the golden-number suite, generate an
# anonymised fixture instead (PRD v2 §23.3).
#
# To include it anyway, delete these two lines and commit deliberately.
Assets/

Docs/KPN - API Payload*.docx
deploy/env/secrets.local.env
# Any local variant/backup of it — these hold live client secrets.
deploy/env/secrets.local.env.*
# staging secrets - filled on servers, never committed
deploy/env/secrets.staging.env
deploy/staging/db.env
deploy/staging/staging.env
deploy/staging/secrets.staging.env
# Filled connection values for the ApsaraDB migration, plus the dumps and
# baselines the scripts produce. The dump holds every row of the dataset.
deploy/migrate/migrate.env
deploy/migrate/*.dump
deploy/migrate/*.dump.sha256

# Production values filled on the servers (security review SEC-S-33). The
# templates (production.env, *.example) stay tracked; filled copies never are.
deploy/production/secrets.production.env
deploy/production/fe-build.env
deploy/production/*.filled.env
**/fe-build.env
# Database password files and dumps made during migrations/seeding.
*.pgpass
**/pgpass
*.dump
pct-export*.tar
